C*******************************************************************************
C
C                          IWFM DEMAND CALCULATOR (IDC)
C                              *** Version 2.1 ***
C
C*******************************************************************************
C
C               CROP SEASONAL EFFICIENCY DATA FILE
C
C
C             Project : CALSIM 3.0 Development
C             Filename: IrigEfficiency.dat
C
C*******************************************************************************
C                           File Description
C
C   This data file contains the seasonal crop efficiency for each crop in each
C   subregion.
C
C*******************************************************************************
C                 Seasonal Crop Efficiency Data Specifications
C
C
C   DSSFL  ; The name of the DSS file for data input (maximum 100 characters);
C             * Leave blank if DSS file is not used for data input
C
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C         VALUE                                      DESCRIPTION
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
         .\inputDSS\CS3_MSMR_IRREFF.dss                 / DSSFL (DSS input data taken from CalSim-III Hydrology Development Project report Table 10-5 Irrigation Efficiencies for Demand Units in the Sacramento River Hydrologic Region)
C-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C                         Seasonal Crop Efficiency Data
C                            (READ FROM THIS FILE)
C
C   List the seasonal crop efficinecy data below, if it will not be read from
C   a DSS file (i.e. DSSFL is left blank above).
C
C   TIME ;  Time
C   IR   ;  Region number
C   CREFF;  Crop efficiency for a particular crop at the specified time.
C             If no irrigation is required, enter 0.
C
C----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C  TIME   IR     CREFF[1]  CREFF[2]  CREFF[3]  .....  CREFF[NCROP]
C----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C			      AL	AP	CO	CR	CU	DB	FI	GR	OG	OR	PA	PO	RI	SB	SF	SO	TH	TM	TR	VI
*10/31/4000_24:00       1    0.69    0.72    0.69       0       0       0       0       0       0    0.74       0    0.76       0    0.72
C----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
C                     Pathnames for Seasonal Crop Efficiency Data
C                             (READ FROM DSS FILE)
C
C   List the pathnames for seasonal crop efficiency data below, if it will be read
C   from a DSS file (i.e. DSSFL is specified above).
C
C   The pathnames should be listed for each subregion and crop type combination.
C   They should be listed in the order given in the example below.
C
C   * Example [simulation includes 3 agricultural crops]
C
C       IR     CRTYPE      PATH
C        1        1       (pathname[1])             => Sub-region 1; crop 1; seasonal crop efficiency
C        1        2       (pathname[2])             => Sub-region 1; crop 2; seasonal crop efficiency
C        1        3       (pathname[3])             => Sub-region 1; crop 3; seasonal crop efficiency
C        2        1       (pathname[4])             => Sub-region 2; crop 1; seasonal crop efficiency
C        2        2       (pathname[5])             => Sub-region 2; crop 2; seasonal crop efficiency
C        2        3       (pathname[6])             => Sub-region 2; crop 3; seasonal crop efficiency
C        .        .            .
C        .        .            .
C        .        .            .
C       NREGN     1       (pathname[(3*NREGN)-2])   => Sub-region NREGN; crop 1; seasonal crop efficiency
